  "notes": [
    "gpt-5.6, gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-daybreak-blue-latest carry a promotional price announced through at least 2026-11-21. Check them again after that date.",
    "gpt-daybreak-blue-latest and gpt-daybreak-red-latest are aliases of gpt-5.6-sol and gpt-5.6-cyber; follow them when they move.",
    "claude-sonnet-4-5 and claude-sonnet-4 now have a 200K window. Their long-context premium only prices older history.",
    "o3 keeps its Standard rates of 2/0.5/8 for input/cache reads/output, matching the pricing table and the first table on its model page. A second, unlabeled model-page table lists 1/0.25/4; verify its meaning before changing Standard rates.",
    "gpt-5.6-cyber and gpt-daybreak-red-latest keep their existing long-context premium pending clarification. The model page describes it, but the pricing table leaves long-context rates unpublished.",
    "Pro has no monthly comparison because plan_type pro does not distinguish the published 100, 200 and 500 USD subscriptions.",
    "Business has no monthly comparison because plan_type business does not distinguish annual billing at 20 USD per seat per month from monthly billing at 25 USD per seat per month.",
    "gpt-6-astra and gpt-6.1-sol Ultrafast cost 6x Standard and require app support for a separate speed tier. Schema 1 only represents Standard and Fast.",
    "gpt-5.3-codex-spark has no published API price. Its existing gpt-5.3-codex family fallback (1.75/0.175/14 for input/cache reads/output) is not verified; schema 1 cannot exclude one ID from a family. gpt-oss models have no OpenAI token price and are excluded.",
    "gpt-5.4-cyber retired on 2026-10-01 and is still within the 91-day history window, but no token price is published in the reviewed official pages. It remains unpriced.",
    "gpt-4-1106-preview retired on 2026-10-23 and is still within the 91-day history window, but has no model-specific price in the reviewed official pages. The current deprecations page no longer lists the previously conflicting 2026-03-26 date for this ID. Its existing gpt-4 family fallback (30/30/60 for input/cache reads/output) is not verified; schema 1 cannot exclude one ID from a family.",
    "OpenAI publishes separate 30-minute and 12-hour cache writes for GPT-6 Astra, GPT-6.1 Sol, GPT-6.1 Terra, GPT-6 Sol, GPT-6 Luna and the GPT-5.6 family. cacheWrite uses the published 30-minute rate. The 12-hour rate is twice that rate; Codex logs currently expose only one cache-write token count, so separate retention pricing requires app support.",
    "GPT-6.1 Sol subscription usage in Codex and ChatGPT Work has no long-context surcharge, unlike its API price above 272K input tokens. This list estimates API value, not subscription allowance consumption.",
    "OpenCode Zen now redirects to OpenCode Console Models. Console is pay-as-you-go with prepaid workspace credits and no seat fee; credit purchases add 4.6% plus 0.31 USD. These fees are not token prices and are not included in this list.",
    "OpenCode Console publishes different rates from the direct APIs: gpt-5, gpt-5-codex, gpt-5.1 and gpt-5.1-codex use 1.07/0.107/8.50 USD per MTok for input/cache reads/output, versus 1.25/0.125/10 direct; claude-sonnet-5-5 cache reads cost 0.20 versus 0.10 direct. Keep direct rates here. Console also prices gpt-5.3-codex-spark at 1.75/0.175/14, which does not establish an OpenAI direct price.",
    "OpenCode Go costs 10 USD/month, Go Plus 40 USD/month, and Go Teams 20 USD/member/month. For each of gpt-6-luna, gpt-5.6-luna and claude-haiku-5-5, monthly included usage is 15/60/20 USD respectively across those plans, with 20% available per five hours and 50% per week. Their published token rates match the direct APIs. Extra Usage can charge the Console balance after an allowance is exhausted; it starts enabled on Go Teams. Schema 1 does not represent these plans or allowances.",
    "OpenCode initially prefers the list's API value for a known model, even over a recorded zero; unknown models can use a recorded charge. Positive reported fallback charges already stored are preserved during repricing. Neither path reconstructs Go allowance consumption or the full provider invoice.",
    "Copilot uses GitHub AI Credits at 0.01 USD each. Pro costs 10 USD/month with 1500 included credits (1000 base plus 500 flex); Pro+ costs 39 with 7000 (3900 plus 3100); Max costs 100 with 20000 (10000 plus 10000). Free and Student have unspecified credit allowances in the reviewed tables. Flex allotments can change and credits do not roll over.",
    "Copilot Business costs 19 USD/seat/month and contributes 1900 credits to a shared pool; Enterprise costs 39 and contributes 3900. Copilot access has no included allowance: it has no additional seat charge for licensed GitHub Enterprise Cloud users or costs 10 USD/seat/month for Copilot Standalone. Additional usage is billed at the published token rates after allowances are exhausted, subject to budgets. These plans and credit pools are not supported by the app's plan objects.",
    "Copilot prices gpt-5.6-luna long context above 200K input tokens, versus 272K in the direct OpenAI API. The app uses the direct API threshold. Copilot's paid-plan auto-selection discount is 10% in Chat and cloud agent; Fusion has a 30% discount through 2026-11-30. Review after that date. The app does not apply these discounts, credits or GitHub Actions charges for code review.",
    "Existing annual Copilot Pro/Pro+ subscriptions may retain legacy request-based billing: 300/1500 premium requests monthly, 0.04 USD per additional request, and model-specific request multipliers. Those multipliers are not API fast-mode prices and must not be stored as fastMultiplier.",
    "Models outside Anthropic/OpenAI remain outside this list's coverage, including Gemini, Grok, MAI-Code, Kimi, GLM, DeepSeek, Qwen, MiniMax, MiMo, Muse, Mistral, LongCat, Step, Hy, Nemotron and anonymous/free models in OpenCode or Copilot. Do not substitute another manufacturer's price. OpenCode's Gemini 4 Argon 50% promotion ends 2026-11-30; Copilot's Gemini 4 Argon promotion ends 2026-12-01 and Gemini 3.8 Flash promotion ends 2026-12-31. Review the provider catalogs after these dates.",
    "Gemini 4 Argon standard prices per million tokens are $2 input, $10 output including thinking, and $0.10 cacheRead through 2026-11-30, rising to $4/$20/$0.20 on 2026-12-01, with no long-context surcharge. Other Gemini prices are Google's standard paid tier through 2026-12-31; they rise on 2027-01-01. gemini-3.7-flash has no published price and takes the equal gemini-3.6-flash and gemini-3.8-flash rate. Antigravity's gemini-pro-default is read as gemini-3.1-pro."
  ],
